  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Thousands of people displaced by floods in Burundi</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">More than 10,000 people have been displaced by devastating floods following heavy rains that have battered parts of Burundi in the recent weeks. Individuals from the rural area of Gatumba, in the province of Bujumbura, have been forced to seek shelter in schools, churches or sometimes in improvised makeshift shelters by the roadside. In addition to losing their homes, many have lost their livelihoods as the flooding has destroyed crops and damaged businesses.</narrative>
  </description>
